        ],
        "category": "Triggers",
        "description": "Real-time Telegram Bot trigger — auto-registers a webhook with Telegram and replies to incoming messages instantly",
        "inputParams": [
          {
            "label": "Bot Token",
            "name": "botToken",
            "type": "password",
            "placeholder": "e.g. 123456789:AABBccdd...",
            "description": "Your Telegram Bot Token from @BotFather. Keep this secret!",
            "id": "telegramTrigger_0-input-botToken-password"
          },
          {
            "label": "How to Use",
            "name": "howToUse",
            "type": "string",
            "default": "",
            "optional": true,
            "additionalParams": true,
            "hint": {
              "label": "Setup Guide",
              "value": "\n## ✈️ Telegram Bot Setup & Token Guide\n\n### Step 1: Get Bot Token from @BotFather\n1. Open Telegram app and search for **@BotFather**.\n2. Send `/newbot` and follow the prompts to choose a bot name and username.\n3. Copy the **HTTP API Bot Token** provided (e.g. `123456789:ABCdefGhIJKlmNo...`).\n4. Paste the token into the **Bot Token** field below.\n\n### Step 2: Activate & Auto-Register Webhook\n1. Toggle the workflow to **ACTIVE** in the canvas header!\n2. MicroMind automatically registers your Webhook (`https://core.aimicromind.com/telegram-webhook/{chatflowId}`) with Telegram's API via `setWebhook`.\n\n### Step 3: Test Live\n1. Open your new bot in Telegram and click **Start** or send a message.\n2. The bot will answer in real-time!\n\n*(Note: For group chats, disable privacy in @BotFather via `/setprivacy` ➔ `Disable`)*\n"
            },
            "description": "Open \"Additional Parameters\" to see the full setup guide.",
            "id": "telegramTrigger_0-input-howToUse-string"
          }
        ],
        "inputAnchors": [],
        "inputs": {
          "howToUse": ""
        },
        "outputAnchors": [
          {
            "name": "output",
            "label": "Output",
            "type": "options",
            "description": "The text content of the incoming Telegram message.",
            "options": [
              {
                "id": "telegramTrigger_0-output-text-string",
                "name": "text",
